# Free drawing becomes a shape: a group on the whiteboard (Inbox/Drawing.canvas, which
# tests/drive.rs writes first) holds a placed circle and a rectangle turned 30°. With the group
# selected, S opens the shape editor on one shape of both, each part where it was: the circle is
# still round (an ellipse of the new box, which is wider than tall), the turned rectangle a closed
# path of its four corners. Saved, it is the workspace's shape drawing1.
size 140x44
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace
keys w
wait-for whiteboards · type to filter
type Drawing
keys enter
wait-for whiteboard Drawing
keys tab
wait-for group · Drawing
keys S
wait-for shape editor · drawing1 (new)
expect circle: ellipse
expect rect: path, 4 vertices, closed
keys ctrl+s
wait-for saved drawing1 in .cold-lava/shapes.toml
keys q
wait-for whiteboard Drawing
keys q
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
keys q
exits 0
